

>> Involved tech

> Lens types
* Pancake Lens
* Aspheric Glass Lens
    - Heavy
* Glass lens
    + No reflections/God-rays/glare
    + No tunnel-vision?
    + Better durability and scratch-resistance
    - Heavy
> Display technologies
* Micro-OLED
    + High pixel density
    + True blacks and great contrast ratios
    - Expensive (still new)
    - Manufacturing is limited to 1.5" panels (since it's still new), meaning small FoV
* QLED
    + High brightness (200 nits); means high color-range
    ~ Backlit, but if used with mini-LED backpanels, it can use local-dimming (back-lights can be turned-off) for True-blacks 
* LCD
    

>> Human-limits
! (unverified) Human-vision is normally around 60 pixels-per-degree - above headsets' output, but not by much
